### 3. An upper bound for the number of sunny lines  

#### 3.1 General observations  

- **Quote:** “A non‑sunny line is either vertical, horizontal, or of slope –1. Horizontal and slope –1 lines also meet each column in at most one point, while a vertical line meets a whole column.”  
